{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/379974-limits-of-raw-materials","id":379974,"title":"Limits of Raw Materials","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-01-24T04:32:01-08:00","id":379974,"title":"Limits of Raw Materials","content":"I wanted to know what the limits on Raw Materials might be ?<br /> <br /> I had a player use it to try and get uranium 233 to blow up a city.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T09:30:19-08:00","id":380231,"title":"","content":"THe Limits on Raw Materials are!<br /> <br /> 1)Common Sense. Always Common Sense. If a player really wants Uranium, he can get it....at a compromise roll. I'd suggest giving a -5. But by and large, it's not going to work quite like that.<br /> 2)Size. THis is the actual limit, and why I wouldn't say that his idea is off limit. But it must be equivalent in size.<br /> 3)Resource value of the broken item. THis is me shitting out of my ass, but I think it can serve as a reasonable yardstick for penalties to compromise rolls when it starts pushing the realms of believability.<br /> <br /> In regards to the larger issue, it must be remembered that the item doesn't magically appear out of nowhere-the hack makes it so that the world conspires to have it land near him to pick up.<br /> <br /> My mind as a GM says that it should be possible for the PC's to do what they want to do given the right resources, time, and most importantly challenges. So, yeah, roll for compromise, but otherwise he gets it....alongside the respective world powers freaking out over it and responding in kind, to say nothing of who or what's on it when it ends up in his lap. He could end up caught in a shadow (tug of) war for the the uranium. Not an easy thing to survive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-24T14:21:39-08:00","id":380474,"title":"","content":"is there something that says what size equals what wight ?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1540-basic","name":"Basic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1540_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"777"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-25T14:35:28-08:00","id":381361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Basic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/379974-limits-of-raw-materials?p=380474#post380474\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is there something that says what size equals what wight ?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. Size is, as far as I know, completely seperate from weight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3323-cmwatford","name":"cmwatford","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3323_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"192"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-01-26T04:57:30-08:00","id":381759,"title":"","content":"It is up the GM to decide how it gets in scene. A G-M delivery truck? Terrorist that is just about to be taken out by an anti-terror squad. I would go by the rule of thumb. The more unbelievable the item is to be in scene the more the compromise roll. It doesn't just appear, it comes in the scene by fate. It is also has to be in the demons reach, so in the scene. It is up to the GM to decide how hard it is to get the item. It could be in a cell. Could be guarded. Yes the demon can get the uranium but it can\u2019t be easy as it is not something someone will leave lying around.<br /> It would at least be in a transport truck and grauded wheather mudane or God Machine realated. He would also be hunted down once he has it as no one is going to let some missing uranium stay missing. uranium gives off radiation it can be tracked and much easier for for an angel to find the demon. Having an angel fly past where he is storing it and sensing the uranium would be breaking anyones cover<br /> <br /> <br /> Another example, you use raw materials to summon a gun. There must be an event that made that gun be there. There might be a shoot out right infront of the demon, the police get involved and start putting police tape around. One of the shooters threw his gun in a bush and ran, hoping to get away clean now the police is there. Now the demon has to deal with not only the fact his embed has cuased people to die, but now needs to sneak past the police to get the gun. Also by using the gun his cover might get blamed for the murder.<br /> <br /> Always remeber there must be a reason for the item to appear. Don't be harsh to the player all the time but give them a hickup sometimes to show that the power is out of their control other than getting the item and thinking before spamming a power.<br /> <br /> tl:dr<br /> <br /> uranium is a not something that is going to be lying around for someone to just pick up. There must be an event that caused it to be in scene.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4090-mental-state","name":"Mental-State","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}